    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Track YouTube channel stats weekly in Google Sheets\n\nEvery Monday this workflow pulls public stats for a list of YouTube channels (yours or competitors') and appends one row per channel to a Google Sheet, so you build a week-by-week history without manual checks.\n\n### Who it's for\nCreators, YouTube agencies and marketers who benchmark channels, track competitors or report growth to clients.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every Monday at 8am** starts the run (change the schedule as you like).\n2. **Set channels to track** holds channel URLs, `@handles` or channel IDs.\n3. **Get channel stats from Apify** calls the YouTube Channel Analytics Actor once for all channels: subscribers, total views, video count, average and median views of the last 10 uploads, upload frequency, plus Social Blade grade, 14-day views gained and estimated monthly earnings.\n4. **Format one row per channel** keeps the columns that matter and adds today's date.\n5. **Append rows to Google Sheet** writes the rows. The columns are matched by name.\n\n### Setup steps (5 min)\n1. Create an Apify account and copy your API token (Console > Settings > API & Integrations).\n2. In **Get channel stats from Apify** create a *Header Auth* credential: Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer <your token>`.\n3. Create a Google Sheet with these headers in row 1: `date, channel, handle, subscribers, totalViews, videoCount, avgViewsLast10, medianViewsLast10, uploadsPerWeek, daysSinceLastUpload, viewsGained14d, socialBladeGrade, estMonthlyEarningsUsd, status`. Paste its URL into **Append rows to Google Sheet** and connect your Google account.\n4. Edit the channel list, run once to test, then activate the workflow.\n\n### Customization\nAdd a Slack or Gmail node after the sheet for a weekly summary, or set `includeSocialBlade: false` in the request body to skip Social Blade data.\n\n*Disclosure: I maintain the Apify Actor used here.*",
        "height": 840,
        "width": 600
      },
      "name": "Template overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -660,
        -420
      ]
    },
